---
import { Badge, Button } from "@openmarch/ui";
import CloseUpField from "@/components/directors/CloseUpField.astro";
---

<section
    id="landing"
    class="relative flex h-fit w-full min-w-0 flex-col items-center justify-center gap-16 rounded-[14px] border border-stroke px-8 pt-32 pb-8"
>
    <Badge variant="secondary"
        ><span class="text-accent">For band directors</span> OpenMarch 0.2</Badge
    >
    <h1
        class="text-h1 leading-[130%] max-[580px]:text-h2 max-[580px]:w-full w-[720px] max-w-full tracking-tighter text-center motion-preset-slide-up motion-delay-150"
    >
        Someone else wrote the drill. You make it work on Tuesday.
    </h1>
    <p
        class="text-body w-full max-w-[36rem] text-center leading-loose motion-delay-250"
    >
        A trumpet quits in week three. The block is two short. Set 14 doesn’t
        fit the kids you have. OpenMarch is the free drill app for fixing the
        show you were handed, printing it, and getting it in front of every
        student.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-8 motion-delay-250">
        <a href="https://editor.openmarch.com">
            <Button>Open in your browser</Button>
        </a>
        <a href="/download">
            <Button variant="secondary">Download</Button>
        </a>
    </div>

    <CloseUpField />
    <p class="text-sub text-text-subtitle max-w-[36rem] pb-8 text-center">
        An illustration of Close up, which works on boxes and outlines in the
        app. <a href="#week" class="text-accent underline"
            >See the real thing below</a
        >.
    </p>

    <div
        class="absolute top-0 motion-preset-fade-lg motion-delay-300 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -z-50 size-[900px] max-[640px]:size-[300px]"
        style="background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--color-accent) 0%, transparent 65%); opacity: 0.4;"
    >
    </div>
</section>
